  "reply": "Almost certainly not. The data runs to 29 October, so there are two days left in the month. The checkout epic SYN-1 Checkout v2: phone wallets and saved cards still has 9 of its 14 items open, and the team has been finishing just under one item a week.\n\nThis thread's workstream has no items yet, so I searched your sources to find the epic. Everything below comes from that search, so I can read these items but can't change them from here.\n\n**Where it stands** (see the count by state below): 5 done, 4 in progress and 5 not started. The in-progress count includes one item that's already open.\n\n**What Oriel's trend projects** (from the chart caption): \"Least-squares line over 7 whole weeks, R² 0.94, 0.8 a week. At that rate the 9 left get there around Jan 14 (Dec 21 – Mar 16, 80%), if no more are added.\" In other words, the best guess is mid-January. Even the earliest end of that range is late December.\n\n**Worth a look** (full list in the table below):\n- Four items haven't been started and haven't moved in about eight weeks: SYN-10 Remove the legacy web-view checkout, SYN-57 Checkout analytics: drop-off by step, SYN-88 Refund to the original payment method when a sailing is cancelled and SYN-98 Apply promo codes at checkout. SYN-99 Save a card for next time is also unstarted. If some of these could move to a later epic, the work left gets smaller.\n- Amara Okafor has three of the open items. Two are in progress: SYN-23 Pay with a phone wallet on the website and SYN-92 Show the fare breakdown before payment.\n- SYN-21 Update the payment declined error message has been in progress for 22 days.\n- SYN-104 Handle 3-D Secure challenges in the native checkout was only started yesterday and has no estimate. SYN-23 Pay with a phone wallet on the website and SYN-99 Save a card for next time have no estimate either.\n\nIf you'd like, I can add the epic and its items to this workstream. Then we could work through what to cut or move here."
}

Claims:
1. The reply gives no finish date, rate or forecast of its own: any it gives is the one Oriel's block caption states, or it says Oriel had too little history to forecast. A yes or no to the question that follows from Oriel's forecast is not one of its own.
